{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().run();\n    }\n\n    void run() {\n        InputReader in = new InputReader(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        \n        int N = in.nextInt();\n        int k = in.nextInt();\n        List<int[]> intervals = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            intervals.add(new int[]{in.nextInt(), in.nextInt()});\n        }\n        intervals.add(new int[]{2 * N, 2 * N});\n        \n        int[][] dp = new int[2][N + 1];\n        Arrays.fill(dp[0], (int)(1e9));\n        dp[0][0] = 0;\n        \n        int cur = 0;\n        for (int[] interval : intervals) {\n            int start = interval[0];\n            int end = interval[1];\n            int len = end - start;\n            \n            int[][] nextDp = new int[2][N + 1];\n            for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {\n                System.arraycopy(dp[i], 0, nextDp[i], 0, N + 1);\n            }\n            \n            for (int j = N; j >= 0; j--) {\n                nextDp[0][j] = (j >= len) ? dp[0][j - len] : (int)(1e9);\n            }\n            cur = end;\n            \n            for (int j = 0; j <= N; j++) {\n                for (int side = 0; side < 2; side++) {\n                    int twoSwaps = getMin(dp[side], j - len, j);\n                    int oneSwap = getMin(dp[1 - side], j - len, j);\n                    int noSwap = (side == 1) ? dp[side][j] : dp[side][j - len];\n                    nextDp[side][j] = Math.min(twoSwaps + 2, Math.min(oneSwap + 1, noSwap));\n                }\n            }\n            \n            dp = nextDp;\n        }\n        \n        int ans = Math.min(dp[0][N], dp[1][N]);\n        if (ans >= (int)(1e9)) {\n            out.println(\"Hungry\");\n        } else {\n            out.println(\"Full\");\n            out.println(ans);\n        }\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    private int getMin(int[] arr, int l, int r) {\n        if (r < 0) return (int)(1e9);\n        int min = (int)(1e9);\n        for (int i = Math.max(0, l); i <= r; i++) {\n            min = Math.min(min, arr[i]);\n        }\n        return min;\n    }\n\n    static class InputReader {\n        private BufferedReader reader;\n        private StringTokenizer tokenizer;\n\n        public InputReader(InputStream stream) {\n            reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(stream), 32768);\n            tokenizer = null;\n        }\n\n        public String next() {\n            while (tokenizer == null || !tokenizer.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                try {\n                    tokenizer = new StringTokenizer(reader.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(e);\n                }\n            }\n            return tokenizer.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        public int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef getMin(arr, l, r):\n    if r < 0:\n        return int(1e9)\n    min_val = int(1e9)\n    for i in range(max(0, l), r + 1):\n        min_val = min(min_val, arr[i])\n    return min_val\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    k = int(input_data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    \n    intervals = []\n    for _ in range(k):\n        start = int(input_data[idx])\n        end = int(input_data[idx + 1])\n        idx += 2\n        intervals.append([start, end])\n    \n    intervals.append([2 * N, 2 * N])\n    \n    dp = [[int(1e9)] * (N + 1) for _ in range(2)]\n    dp[0][0] = 0\n    \n    cur = 0\n    for interval in intervals:\n        start = interval[0]\n        end = interval[1]\n        length = end - start\n        \n        next_dp = [row[:] for row in dp]\n        \n        for j in range(N, -1, -1):\n            if j >= length:\n                next_dp[0][j] = dp[0][j - length]\n            else:\n                next_dp[0][j] = int(1e9)\n        \n        cur = end\n        \n        for j in range(N + 1):\n            for side in range(2):\n                two_swaps = getMin(dp[side], j - length, j)\n                one_swap = getMin(dp[1 - side], j - length, j)\n                if side == 1:\n                    no_swap = dp[side][j]\n                else:\n                    no_swap = dp[side][j - length] if j - length >= 0 else int(1e9)\n                next_dp[side][j] = min(two_swaps + 2, min(one_swap + 1, no_swap))\n        \n        dp = next_dp\n    \n    ans = min(dp[0][N], dp[1][N])\n    if ans >= int(1e9):\n        print(\"Hungry\")\n    else:\n        print(\"Full\")\n        print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.83428253675811e-05, -8.344646